{title: Hosanna, Loud Hosanna}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune ELLACOMBE}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Ho[C]sanna, [G]loud ho[Am]san[G]na, the [F]little [G]children [C]sang[**]
Through [C]pillared [G]court and [Am]tem[G]ple, the [F]lovely [G]anthem [C]rang[**]
To [C]Jesus, [**]who had [G]blessed [**]them, close [C]folded [**]to his [G]breast[**]
The [C]children [G]sang their [Am]prai[G]ses, the [F]simplest [G]and the [C]best[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
From [C]Oli[G]vet they [Am]fol[G]lowed 'mid [F]an e[G]xultant [C]crowd[**]
The [C]victor [G]palm branch [Am]wa[G]ving and [F]chanting [G]clear and [C]loud[**]
The [C]Lord of [**]earth and [G]hea[**]ven rode [C]on in [**]lowly [G]state[**]
Nor [C]scorned that [G]little [Am]chil[G]dren should [F]on his [G]bidding [C]wait[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
"Ho[C]sanna [G]in the [Am]high[G]est!" That [F]ancient [G]song we [C]sing[**]
For [C]Christ is [G]our Re[Am]dee[G]mer, the [F]Lord of [G]heaven our [C]King[**]
O [C]may we [**]ever [G]praise [**]him with [C]heart and [**]life and [G]voice[**]
And [C]in his [G]blissful [Am]pre[G]sence e[F]ternal[G]ly re[C]joice[**]!
{end_of_verse}
